<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>t1a10-Events-by-Sara</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg-color: #0d1117;
            --card-bg: #161b22;
            --border-color: #30363d;
            --accent-primary: #58a6ff;
            --accent-secondary: #bc8cff;
            --text-color: #c9d1d9;
            --text-muted: #8b949e;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: var(--bg-color);
            color: var(--text-color);
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 40px auto;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        }

        h2 {
            color: var(--accent-primary);
            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border-color);
            padding-bottom: 10px;
        }

        a {
            color: var(--accent-secondary);
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: 600;
        }
        a:hover {
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        .card {
            background-color: var(--card-bg);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }

        input[type="text"], select {
            background-color: var(--bg-color);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            color: var(--text-color);
            padding: 8px 12px;
            border-radius: 6px;
            font-size: 14px;
        }

        input[type="button"] {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #238636, #2ea043);
            color: white;
            border: none;
            padding: 10px 18px;
            border-radius: 6px;
            font-weight: bold;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: opacity 0.2s;
        }
        input[type="button"]:hover {
            opacity: 0.9;
        }

        #myDiv01 {
            background-color: var(--bg-color);
            border: 1px dashed var(--accent-primary);
            padding: 12px;
            border-radius: 6px;
            margin-top: 10px;
            font-family: monospace;
            color: var(--accent-primary);
        }

        #myB02 {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 8px 14px;
            background-color: rgba(188, 140, 255, 0.1);
            border-radius: 4px;
            border: 1px solid var(--accent-secondary);
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: all 0.2s;
        }

        .event-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
            gap: 15px;
            margin-top: 15px;
        }

        .event-box {
            background-color: var(--bg-color);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            padding: 12px;
            border-radius: 6px;
            font-size: 13px;
        }

        .log-output {
            color: var(--accent-secondary);
            font-weight: bold;
            margin-top: 5px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h2 align="center">t1a10-Events-by-Sara</h2>
    <a href="https://way2tutorial.com/html/html15_events_handler_list.php">Good reference to HTML Events</a> <br><br> 
    
    <div class="card">
        <input type="text" id="myText01" value="3"><br><br>

        <input type="button" value="Example" onclick="{
        document.getElementById ('myDiv01').innerHTML= document.getElementById('myText01').value}"> <br><br>

        <div id="myDiv01">...</div><br>

        <b id="myB02" onMouseOut="{ 
            document.getElementById ('myB02').innerHTML= 'This is nice.'}" 
            onMouseOver="{ document.getElementById ('myB02').innerHTML = 'This is so cool.'}"> This is Bold</b> <br> <br> 
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Interactive Event Playground (Assignment Tasks)</h3>
        <p>Testing out the requested event handlers with live status logs:</p>
        
        <div class="event-grid">
        
            <div class="event-box" ondblclick="this.style.borderColor='#2ea043'; document.getElementById('log-dbl').innerText='Double-Clicked Success!';">
                <b>ondblclick</b>: Double-click this box.
                <div id="log-dbl" class="log-output">Waiting...</div>
            </div>

            <div class="event-box">
                <b>onfocus / onblur / onchange</b>:<br>
                <input type="text" placeholder="Click me..." 
                       onfocus="this.style.borderColor='#58a6ff'; document.getElementById('log-focus').innerText='Focused!';" 
                       onblur="this.style.borderColor='#30363d'; document.getElementById('log-focus').innerText='Blurred!';"
                       onchange="document.getElementById('log-focus').innerText='Changed to: ' + this.value;">
                <div id="log-focus" class="log-output">Idle</div>
            </div>
            <div class="event-box" onmousemove="document.getElementById('log-move').innerText = 'X: ' + event.clientX + ' Y: ' + event.clientY;">
                <b>onmousemove</b>: Hover over this box.
                <div id="log-move" class="log-output">Coordinates: (0, 0)</div>
            </div>
            <div class="event-box">
                <b>onkeydown</b>: Type a key here.<br>
                <input type="text" placeholder="Press key..." onkeydown="document.getElementById('log-key').innerText='Key pressed: ' + event.key;">
                <div id="log-key" class="log-output">No key pressed</div>
            </div>

            <div class="event-box" draggable="true" ondragstart="document.getElementById('log-drag').innerText='Dragging started!';">
                <b>ondragstart</b>: Drag this text box!
                <div id="log-drag" class="log-output">Ready to drag</div>
            </div>

  
            <div class="event-box" ontouchstart="document.getElementById('log-touch').innerText='Touch Started!';" ontouchend="document.getElementById('log-touch').innerText='Touch Ended!';">
                <b>ontouchstart / ontouchend</b>: Tap/Touch here (Mobile).
                <div id="log-touch" class="log-output">No touch detected</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
